  "id": "off-cells",
  "term": "off cells",
  "definition": "Off cells are brainstem neurons involved in REM sleep control that reduce or stop their activity during REM sleep, in contrast to REM-on cells that become active. In the pons, the best identified REM off cells include serotonin-containing neurons in the dorsal raphe and norepinephrine-containing neurons in the locus coeruleus.",
